{# ============================================================================
   HYPER · PLACEHOLDER CARD
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   What a section shows on a fresh install, before the merchant has picked any
   products / collections / articles. Without it a new store opens on rows of
   empty white space and the merchant cannot tell whether the section is broken
   or simply unfilled.

   ⚠️  It borrows the REAL card's classes — `.hy-pcard-*`, `.hy-coll-tile`,
   `.hy-post` — so the placeholder occupies exactly the space the real thing
   will, and the merchant is looking at the true layout while they work. Only
   `--ph` modifiers differ.

   ⚠️  Inert on purpose:
     · no `x-data`, so no cart component is created for a product that has no id
     · every link is `href="#"` with `@click.prevent`, so a click cannot land on
       a 404 or leave the page
     · `aria-hidden="true"` and `data-hy-placeholder`, so screen readers skip it
       and no script can ever mistake it for stock

   Locals:
     kind        'product' (default) · 'collection' · 'article'
     count       how many to draw (default 4)
     image_ratio '2x3' | '3x4' | '4x5' | '1x1' — product/collection only
     variant     'compact' | 'catalog' — passes through to the product card
                 layout, so the placeholder matches whatever the real row uses
     price       the dummy price line, already formatted (default '—')
     wrap        class for a wrapper around each card — 'swiper-slide' when the
                 host is a Swiper, which needs every child to be a slide

   Styling: assets/style.css → "15.29 PLACEHOLDERS".
   ========================================================================= #}

{% set kind = data.kind | default('product') %}
{% set count = data.count | default(4) | int %}
{% set variant = data.variant | default('') %}
{% set phPrice = data.price | default('') %}
{% set wrap = data.wrap | default('') %}

{% set ratio = data.image_ratio | default('2x3') %}
{% if ratio == '1x1' %}{% set ratioVal = '1 / 1' %}
{% elif ratio == '4x5' %}{% set ratioVal = '4 / 5' %}
{% elif ratio == '3x4' %}{% set ratioVal = '3 / 4' %}
{% else %}{% set ratioVal = '2 / 3' %}{% endif %}


{# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The piece. Flat, two tones off the theme's own neutrals, no photograph — it
   has to read as "nothing here yet" at a glance, which a stock photo never
   does. Four shapes so a row of four is not four copies of one; `n` picks by
   index.

   The viewBox is 200×170 — WIDE, and the four subjects were chosen to suit it.
   `.hy-ph-art` sizes by HEIGHT (15.29), so a tall narrow subject drawn here —
   a feeding bottle, say — would come out no wider than a thumb while the piece
   beside it filled the frame, and the row would read as a rendering fault
   rather than as a set. A romper with its sleeves out, a rattle lying on its
   side, a pair of booties and a bear all fill it.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- #}
{% macro piece(n) %}
  <svg class="hy-ph-art" viewBox="0 0 200 170" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
    {% set i = n % 4 %}
    {% if i == 0 %}
      {# رومبر — a short romper. The LEGS are what make it read as babywear
         rather than as a shirt: a bodysuit's snap crotch is a straight hem at
         this size, and a straight hem on a wide torso is a top. #}
      <rect class="hy-ph-fill" x="8" y="40" width="54" height="36" rx="17"/>
      <rect class="hy-ph-fill" x="138" y="40" width="54" height="36" rx="17"/>
      <rect class="hy-ph-fill" x="50" y="30" width="100" height="80" rx="24"/>
      <rect class="hy-ph-fill" x="54" y="92" width="42" height="54" rx="18"/>
      <rect class="hy-ph-fill" x="104" y="92" width="42" height="54" rx="18"/>
      <ellipse class="hy-ph-tint" cx="100" cy="36" rx="21" ry="10"/>
      <rect class="hy-ph-tint" x="62" y="96" width="76" height="16" rx="8"/>
    {% elif i == 1 %}
      {# خشخيشة — a rattle. The ring at the end is a TINT disc inside a fill
         disc, not a hole: both tones are translucent and sit on a card whose
         ground is not always the same colour, so a real cut-out would show
         whatever happens to be behind it. #}
      <circle class="hy-ph-fill" cx="70" cy="60" r="44"/>
      <circle class="hy-ph-tint" cx="70" cy="60" r="21"/>
      <rect class="hy-ph-fill" x="94" y="84" width="46" height="26" rx="13"
            transform="rotate(38 94 84)"/>
      <circle class="hy-ph-fill" cx="146" cy="126" r="31"/>
      <circle class="hy-ph-tint" cx="146" cy="126" r="16"/>
    {% elif i == 2 %}
      {# حذاء بيبي — a pair of booties, seen from the side.

         ONE path each, not a leg rectangle plus a foot rectangle. Both tones are
         translucent, so two fill shapes that overlap darken where they cross —
         the ankle would have shown as a bruise across the join. The cuff is the
         other tone, which is why it may sit on top.

         Drawn tall — 18→150 of the 170 box — so the pair carries the same
         weight as the bear beside it. At the height it was first drawn the two
         boots read as a smaller object rather than as a different one. #}
      <path class="hy-ph-fill" d="M30 26h14a16 16 0 0 1 16 16v58h16a25 25 0 0 1 0 50H30a16 16 0 0 1-16-16V42a16 16 0 0 1 16-16Z"/>
      <rect class="hy-ph-tint" x="6" y="18" width="62" height="24" rx="12"/>
      <path class="hy-ph-fill" d="M124 26h14a16 16 0 0 1 16 16v58h16a25 25 0 0 1 0 50h-46a16 16 0 0 1-16-16V42a16 16 0 0 1 16-16Z"/>
      <rect class="hy-ph-tint" x="100" y="18" width="62" height="24" rx="12"/>
    {% else %}
      {# دبدوب — a bear. Ears before the head, and the limbs before the body, so
         each pair meets in a joint instead of showing a seam: both tones are
         translucent and two shapes of one tone darken where they cross. #}
      <circle class="hy-ph-fill" cx="68" cy="36" r="18"/>
      <circle class="hy-ph-fill" cx="132" cy="36" r="18"/>
      <rect class="hy-ph-fill" x="24" y="88" width="42" height="30" rx="15"/>
      <rect class="hy-ph-fill" x="134" y="88" width="42" height="30" rx="15"/>
      <rect class="hy-ph-fill" x="60" y="84" width="80" height="70" rx="32"/>
      <circle class="hy-ph-fill" cx="100" cy="56" r="41"/>
      <ellipse class="hy-ph-tint" cx="100" cy="66" rx="19" ry="14"/>
      <ellipse class="hy-ph-tint" cx="100" cy="120" rx="23" ry="21"/>
    {% endif %}
  </svg>
{% endmacro %}


{% for n in range(0, count) %}
{% if wrap %}<div class="{{ wrap }}">{% endif %}

  {# ═══════════════ product ═══════════════ #}
  {% if kind == 'product' %}
    <article class="hy-pcard hy-pcard--ph {{ 'hy-pcard--compact' if variant == 'compact' }} {{ 'hy-pcard--catalog' if variant == 'catalog' }}"
             style="--pcard-ratio: var(--hy-card-ratio, {{ ratioVal }});"
             data-hy-placeholder aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="hy-pcard-frame">
        <a href="#" @click.prevent class="hy-pcard-media hy-ph-media" tabindex="-1">
          {{ piece(n) }}
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="hy-pcard-info">
        {# The catalog card leads with a category line. The order of the three
           is a flex `order` in 15.9.1, not this markup order — same rule as the
           real card, so the placeholder cannot drift out of step with it. #}
        {% if variant == 'catalog' %}
          <span class="hy-pcard-eyebrow">{{ t('common.placeholder_collection') }}</span>
        {% endif %}
        <div class="hy-pcard-prices">
          <span class="hy-price">{{ phPrice if phPrice else t('common.placeholder_price') }}</span>
        </div>
        <span class="hy-pcard-name hy-clamp-2">{{ t('common.placeholder_product') }}</span>
      </div>
    </article>

  {# ═══════════════ collection ═══════════════ #}
  {% elif kind == 'collection' %}
    <a href="#" @click.prevent class="hy-coll-tile hy-coll-tile--ph"
       style="--coll-ratio: {{ ratioVal }};"
       data-hy-placeholder aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">
      <span class="hy-ph-media">{{ piece(n) }}</span>
      <div class="hy-coll-foot">
        <span class="hy-coll-name">{{ t('common.placeholder_collection') }}</span>
      </div>
    </a>

  {# ═══════════════ article ═══════════════ #}
  {% else %}
    <a href="#" @click.prevent class="hy-post hy-post--stacked hy-post--ph"
       data-hy-placeholder aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">
      <div class="hy-post-media hy-ph-media">{{ piece(n) }}</div>
      <div class="hy-post-body">
        <div class="hy-post-meta"><span>{{ t('common.placeholder_date') }}</span></div>
        <h3 class="hy-post-title hy-clamp-2">{{ t('common.placeholder_article') }}</h3>
        <p class="hy-post-excerpt hy-clamp-2">{{ t('common.placeholder_excerpt') }}</p>
      </div>
    </a>
  {% endif %}

{% if wrap %}</div>{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
